winewayland: position GPU child windows and map input from the cropped window's real origin (Premiere black line)

A maximized Premiere keeps a window that hangs 5 px off the monitor, and the frame-spill crop shows it from an inner
origin, so surface-local (0,0) is window (5,0). GPU child windows (the Program Monitor) were still placed from the
window origin: 5 px right, leaving a black strip down their left edge, and pointer input landed 5 px left of the
pointer. The applied crop origin is now recorded (wayland_surface_content_origin) and used for client and owned
subsurface positions, pointer motion, confine and warp, tablet and Wintab positions, and drag-and-drop. Kill switch
NEUTRON_CROP_ORIGIN=0. Harness: preserved-fixes/harnesses/ptrcheck.c (overhang0) and clipped-gpu-child.c (overhang).

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_data_device.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_data_device.c
@@ -1191,11 +1191,13 @@
     if ((surface = data->wayland_surface))
     {
         RECT *window_rect = &surface->window.rect;
+        int ox, oy;   /* NEUTRON: frame-spill crop origin, see wayland_surface_content_origin */
+        wayland_surface_content_origin(surface, &ox, &oy);
         wayland_surface_coords_to_window(surface, wl_fixed_to_double(x_w),
                                          wl_fixed_to_double(y_w),
                                          (int *)&pt->x, (int *)&pt->y);
-        pt->x += window_rect->left;
-        pt->y += window_rect->top;
+        pt->x += window_rect->left + ox;
+        pt->y += window_rect->top + oy;
     }
     wayland_win_data_release(data);
 }
